---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="stephfh.dev – Used things">
    <h1>Used things</h1>
    <p>Inspired by <a href="https://uses.tech">Wes Bos' uses.tech</a>
        <br/>
        As a developer you use a lot of different tools. There are a lot of options out there and
        everyone has their own set of tools, below I’ve listed some of the tools in my setup.
    </p>

    <h2>👩‍💻 Tech</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>MacBook Pro, Retina 2015 (15-inch)</li>
        <li>Magic Keyboard</li>
        <li>Magic Trackpad</li>
        <li>LG Ultrawide 4k @ 34"</li>
        <li>iPhone 14 Plus (RED)</li>
        <li>AirPods Pro</li>
        <li>CCZ Melody in ears</li>
        <li>HyperX QuadCast Microphone</li>
        <li>Creality Ender 3 3D-Printer</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>💻 Software</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Editor: JetBrains PhpStorm and for quick edits neovim</li>
        <li>Font: JetBrains Mono with ligatures enabled (yes, I'm one of those) and NerdFonts patch</li>
        <li>Terminal: Hyper, Shell: zsh with ohmyzsh</li>
        <li>Browser: As I'm  a web developer, technically all of them. For browsing mostly Safari (MacOS and iOS)</li>
        <li>Design: Figma</li>
        <li>Mail: Apple Mail</li>
        <li>Database Management: Datagrip (within PhpStorm)</li>
        <li>Recording: OBS</li>
        <li>Brain dump: Obsidian</li>
        <li>Misc: Raycast</li>
    </ul>
</Layout>
